Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Repository Stitch Projection Capacity Successor Binding Revision 0.1 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] bc4078c9-620e-49f6-844d-1b0c0bae9e6a
@ [canonical_uuid] bd6411fc-4854-4996-b1af-4e94c3abe567

& [Problem]
  + published RSP formation copied a candidate-pool ceiling of sixteen into selected-set capacity while the published selector and corrected stitch compiler admit at most eight selected declarations

& [Decision]
  + add one signed successor binding that narrows only RSP-007 selected cardinality from sixteen to eight and preserves all other RSP semantics

& [WhyNow]
  + capacity revision 0.2 is complete and CSR2-016 makes this binding the only authorized prerequisite before preserved RSP implementation can resume

& [Rejected]
  + rewrite the published RSP specification because that would destroy historical identity and hash evidence
  + raise stitch capacity to sixteen because verified 8192-byte constraints and selector semantics do not support it
  + lower upstream candidate-pool capacity because selection may still evaluate sixteen candidates while returning at most eight
  + treat count admission as byte admission because the downstream projection ceiling remains independently enforced

& [Consequence]
  + the paused adapter can resume against an exact eight-selected boundary with a nine-selected adversary and no expansion of provider model prompt execution or effect authority
